// endpoint_subscribe_merge_queue.proto — SubscribeMergeQueue: tell one
// workspace's agent about a merge queue's changes as they happen, so it can
// wait on the queue (land after the queue drains, report a landing to the
// user) without polling it. AGENT API section.
//
// DELIVERY: each notice is submitted to the subscriber's session as a
// deferred prompt of origin
// conversation.v1.PromptOrigin.PROMPT_ORIGIN_MERGE_QUEUE_NOTICE, the same
// path an async merge's handback takes: it waits behind a running turn, wakes
// an idle agent, and the feed draws no row for it. Every notice names the
// changes it reports and carries the queue AS IT STANDS AFTER THEM
// (MergeQueueStatus).
//
// SCOPE: a workspace holds AT MOST ONE subscription per scope -- one
// repository's queue, or every repository's -- and subscribing again in a
// scope it holds replaces that subscription's detail. A scoped and an
// unscoped subscription may stand together; a change both admit is delivered
// once, as one notice.
//
// LIFETIME: a subscription ends when its workspace unsubscribes in its scope,
// and when the workspace closes, however it closes (closed, killed, nuked, or
// closed by its own landing); re-opening the workspace does not restore it.
// It is DURABLE across a daemon restart and a handover: a landing's own deploy
// restarts the daemon, so a subscription that a restart dropped would end at
// the very change it exists to report. A change made while no daemon serves
// is never reported; the next notice's snapshot carries its effect.
//
// NOTHING SLIPS BETWEEN READING AND FOLLOWING. The answer carries the queues
// in scope as they stand when the subscription is taken (MergeQueueStatus,
// the same status every notice carries), and every change after that answer
// is noticed.

